{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_32cef6356edb9e830cac1245e4ff02dd3b8a44a69f5113160f33ecb49978dee3", "title": "Robert H. Goddard", "text": "Robert Hutchings Goddard (October 5, 1882 – August 10, 1945) was an American engineer, professor, physicist, and inventor who is credited with creating and building the world's first liquid-fueled rocket. Goddard successfully launched his model on March 16, 1926, ushering in an era of space flight and innovation. He and his team launched 34 rockets between 1926 and 1941, achieving altitudes as high as 2.6 km and speeds as fast as 885 km/h (550 mph).", "score": 26.7708}, {"id": "hp_doc_5d32cac83c1d43d4ea0dbae30b92c65b9539a6467d349967e87cd5d10b30a1f1", "title": "Goddard Rocket Launching Site", "text": "The Goddard Rocket Launching Site is a National Historic Landmark commemorating the launch site of the world's first successful liquid-fueled rocket. It is located at 20 Upland Street, Auburn, Massachusetts, within the Pakachoag Golf Course. The launch site is indicated with two markers accessible to visitors while the golf course is open. It is at the \"9th Fairway, between Tee and Green,\" of the Pakachoag Golf Course.", "score": 24.8905}, {"id": "hp_doc_74e1c1016681235bf1ac40e341da174bd04b1cb054d188cdda31dd20793bf288", "title": "Friedrich Zander", "text": "Friedrich Zander (Russian: Фридрих Артурович Цандер \"Fridrikh Arturovich Tsander\". Latvian: \"Frīdrihs Canders\" , 11 August [O.S. 23 August] 1887 – 28 March 1933), was a Baltic German pioneer of rocketry and spaceflight in the Russian Empire and the Soviet Union. He designed the first liquid-fueled rocket to be launched in the Soviet Union, GIRD-X, and made many important theoretical contributions to the road to space.", "score": 21.7183}], "remaining_searches": 2}
